.nh
.TH "GUMROAD" "1" "Sep 2026" "Gumroad" "Gumroad CLI"

.SH NAME
gumroad-admin-purchases-reassign - Reassign every purchase from one buyer email to another


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgumroad admin purchases reassign [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Reassign every purchase made by --from to --to. Subscriptions and the
underlying purchaser_id (when --to belongs to an existing user) are
updated as part of the move, and a grouped receipt is sent to --to.

.PP
This affects ALL successful purchases for --from. There is no way to
filter to a single purchase from this command.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--from\fP=""
	Source buyer email (required)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for reassign

.PP
\fB--to\fP=""
	Destination buyer email (required)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging to stderr

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Preview mutating requests without executing them

.PP
\fB--jq\fP=""
	Filter JSON output with a jq expression

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output as JSON

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable color output

.PP
\fB--no-image\fP[=false]
	Disable image rendering

.PP
\fB--no-input\fP[=false]
	Disable interactive prompts

.PP
\fB--non-interactive\fP[=false]
	Run in explicit CI/agent mode

.PP
\fB--page-delay\fP=0s
	Wait between paginated --all requests (e.g. 200ms, 1s)

.PP
\fB--plain\fP[=false]
	Output as plain tab-separated text

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Suppress non-essential output

.PP
\fB--yes\fP[=false]
	Skip confirmation prompts


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  gumroad admin purchases reassign --from old@example.com --to new@example.com
  gumroad admin purchases reassign --from old@example.com --to new@example.com --yes
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgumroad-admin-purchases(1)\fP
